# Universal Responsive Rules

## 1. Zero Script Layout Engine

- Never use heavy JavaScript resize loops (`window.addEventListener('resize')`) or client-side layout math engines for device responsiveness.
- All auto-fit properties must rely on native Tailwind CSS viewport utility classes only.

## 2. Structural Scaling Constraints

- Desktop layout states default to horizontal flex arrays (`flex-row`).
- Tablet boundaries (`md:`) trigger grid column adjustments (`grid-cols-2`).
- Mobile profiles (`max-w-md`) force stacked vertical columns (`flex-col`), hide non-essential heavy video monitoring surfaces (`hidden lg:block`), and scale action buttons to full touch-friendly widths (`w-full`).

## 3. Owner Shell

- Mobile: top header bar + hamburger drawer (`block md:hidden`).
- Tablet/desktop: fixed left sidebar (`hidden md:flex md:w-[13.5rem]`).
- `/owner/**` never renders the attendee bottom PNG dock — see `lib/routes.ts`.

## 4. Telemetry Protection

- Camera preview buses, embedded WebRTC publishers, and VU meter canvases are presentation-only on large screens.
- On phone viewports, show text status tokens and action buttons only — no local video elements.
